<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SEC-1-6
TITLE: 1.6 Relationship to PIDKiln

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
PIDKiln [R1] demonstrates that a ~40 USD ESP32 board can run a real kiln, and
this project adopts its proven ideas: a segment-based program model
(`target / ramp / dwell`), dual display and web control, on-device storage with
no external services, a redundant SSR + contactor output stage, and safety
supervision covering runaway, probe failure, SSR failure and insulation
degradation.

Safe Kiln Controller deliberately diverges in the following respects, and these
divergences drive many requirements below:

| Aspect | PIDKiln | Safe Kiln Controller | Driver |
|---|---|---|---|
| Framework | Arduino-ESP32 | ESP-IDF v5.x ([LINK: CON-01]) | Explicit requirement; better test tooling, partition/OTA control, watchdogs |
| MCU | ESP32-WROVER | ESP32-S3 ([LINK: HR-01]) | Explicit requirement |
| TC front-end | MAX31855 (K only, ≤1350 °C) | MAX31856 (K/N/S/R/B/E/J/T, richer fault detection) | Diagnosability, [LINK: SR-04] |
| PID gains | Manually tuned, documented by experiment | Automatic tuning on-device (FR-TUN ([LINK: SEC-3-3])) | Explicit requirement |
| Storage | SPIFFS on internal flash, microSD board recommended | Dedicated raw partitions, fixed slots for programs and run records and a circular ring for the log, no SD card and no filesystem ([LINK: CON-03]) | Explicit requirement |
| Heater current | Optional 30 A/1 V power meter, not used for protection | **Mandatory** current transformer driving relay fail-on / fail-off detection and weld discrimination (FR-CUR ([LINK: SEC-3-12]), [LINK: SR-25]–[LINK: SR-30]) | Explicit requirement; resolves [LINK: OQ-02] |
| Architecture | Arduino sketch, hardware access throughout | Layered, HAL-isolated, host-testable core (TR ([LINK: SEC-7])) | Explicit requirement: design for testability |

No PIDKiln source code is copied. Safe Kiln Controller is licensed GPL-3.0-or-later, the
same licence as PIDKiln, so derivation remains possible in either direction.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
